<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- The entitlements a LOCAL build is signed with. Never a released one:
	     see hyperwave-release.entitlements, which is what
	     scripts/package-macos.sh uses.

	     The two keys below let a debugger attach to a Developer-ID-signed
	     build, and com.apple.security.get-task-allow is an automatic
	     notarization refusal — Apple rejects anything carrying it, reporting
	     only "status: Invalid" unless you go and fetch the log by submission
	     id. If these ever reach a release signature again, that is the
	     symptom to expect.

	     Deliberately near-empty otherwise.
	     Not sandboxed. System audio capture via CoreAudio process taps is
	     gated by a TCC grant (kTCCServiceAudioCapture), not by an
	     entitlement, and it is not clear that taps are permitted under App
	     Sandbox at all. Sandboxing this app would buy nothing and might cost
	     the one feature it has.
	     The two below are development conveniences so a debugger can attach
	     to a Developer-ID-signed build. They should come out of the release
	     entitlements when there is a release.

	     audio-input is here only to match the release file. A local build is
	     not signed with the hardened runtime, so it hears the built-in mic
	     either way; a release is, and without the key it hears nothing from
	     it. See hyperwave-release.entitlements. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.debugger</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.get-task-allow</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
